## 18. Money, Entry Fees, and Prizes

The interface may display configured entry prices and prizes, but the application must not pretend that displaying an amount means a payment has occurred.

If paid entry or real-money prizes are part of the intended product:
- Use a properly integrated payment provider where legally available.
- Validate all payment events on the backend.
- Record transactions securely.
- Prevent duplicate charges and duplicate payouts.
- Reconcile payments against game registrations.
- Implement refunds and cancellation handling where applicable.
- Protect against fraudulent claims and unauthorized balance changes.
- Do not store card details directly unless the appropriate compliant payment infrastructure is in place.

Before enabling real-money gaming, confirm applicable gambling, lottery, payment, age-verification, and data-protection requirements in the target jurisdictions.

If these integrations are not configured, implement a clearly labeled demo or free-play mode rather than presenting simulated transactions as real.

