## 23. Final Acceptance Criteria

The application is ready for further production preparation when:

1. A new user can register and log in.
2. An authenticated user can access the main Bingo screen.
3. The user can generate between one and ten valid random Bingo cards.
4. Generated cards are stored and associated with the correct user and game.
5. The expandable game-information card displays actual configured information.
6. The horizontal called-number history updates correctly.
7. The 75-number board reflects the authoritative game history.
8. Blocked cards are displayed and enforced by the backend.
9. Winning claims are verified by the backend.
10. Confirmed winners are displayed accurately.
11. Multiple clients can synchronize with the same game when realtime support is configured.
12. The header controls, settings, and navigation work correctly.
13. The application handles common errors without crashing.
14. The layout matches the visual direction of the attached screenshots.
15. No critical game rules or security checks depend exclusively on frontend code.

**Final instruction:** Start by inspecting the existing project and the attached screenshots. Then implement the application in a structured, incremental manner. Prioritize functional correctness, secure game logic, and a polished mobile interface. Do not stop after creating a mockup, and do not replace existing working functionality with fake data or nonfunctional buttons. If any backend service is unavailable, explain the missing configuration and implement as much of the working integration as possible.
